          "title": "You'll want to know: வாழ்த்து",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வாழ்த்து (vāḻttu) — \"a good wish\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Straight off vāḻ, 'to live, to flourish', which you had early. To give somebody a vāḻttu is to wish them a life — not luck, not success, but the thing itself."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vāḻttukkaḷ is what a Tamil speaker says where English says \"congratulations\", and it is the kinder sentence of the two: flourishing, offered in the plural, rather than a nod at what you managed to pull off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four, and the fourth one is given rather than felt."
            }
          ]
        },
